# fw_printenv BOOT_ORDER BOOT_A_LEFT BOOT_B_LEFT
BOOT_ORDER=A
BOOT_A_LEFT=3
BOOT_B_LEFT=0

--- reading it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. The install failed at the signature, before writing anything: BOOT_ORDER, BOOT_A_LEFT and
   BOOT_B_LEFT are unchanged, which is FR-019 (verify before the first write) holding by accident
   on a bundle the project itself produced.
2. It is not the clock. The board's clock read 2026-10-29 08:00 (ota-clock raised it at boot),
   inside the certificate's window; the first failure R8 predicted ("not yet valid") did not occur.
3. Cause: the signing certificate has the Code Signing extended key usage only, and RAUC's
   system.conf had no check-purpose, so OpenSSL verified the CMS for S/MIME signing and refused.
   Reproduced on the host from the bundle itself: `openssl cms -verify` on the extracted
   signature fails with the same message by default and succeeds with `-purpose any`, so the
   digest and the chain were fine. Fix: check-purpose=codesign in the board's system.conf,
   which lives in the slot, so the device needs the fixed image before it can install anything.
4. The host-side build could not have found this: `rauc info` in the container stops at the
   bundle mount before it checks the signature, which is why T026 could not verify it either.
5. The marker file in /data survived (SC-006 is not tested yet, nothing was installed).

==========================================================================================
SECOND ATTEMPT, same day, image f95075c (check-purpose=codesign), bundle 44b167e
SHA-256 35515b842cb01b81b886d7258177f3f84df44cad13626c69e98945aa22e8d18e on both ends.
==========================================================================================

# rauc install /data/b.raucb
 10% Checking bundle
rauc-Message: 08:31:15.480: Verifying bundle signature...
 10% Verifying signature
rauc-Message: 08:31:15.850: Verified detached signature by 'O = OTA development, CN = OTA development bundle signing - NOT FOR PRODUCTION'
 20% Verifying signature done.
 20% Checking bundle done.
rauc-event-Message: 08:31:15.870: Installation ba150e64 failed: Failed mounting bundle: Failed creating mount point: Failed creating mount path '/mnt/rauc/bundle': Read-only file system
100% Installing failed.
Installing `/data/b.raucb` failed

--- reading it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. The first fix worked: the signature is verified, by the development signing certificate.
2. The next failure is the read-only slot: RAUC's default mount prefix is /mnt/rauc, which it
   cannot create. Fix: mountprefix=/run/rauc (tmpfs).
3. Found while looking behind it, before the third flash: the kernel has no SquashFS
   (# CONFIG_SQUASHFS is not set). A plain bundle is a squashfs, compressed with gzip, and
   RAUC mounts it with mount(2) type "squashfs" through /dev/loop-control, so the mount would
   have failed next with "squashfs support not enabled in kernel". Fix: CONFIG_SQUASHFS=y and
   CONFIG_SQUASHFS_ZLIB=y; the loop driver is already built in.
4. Both were invisible to the host build for the same reason as the purpose failure: nothing
   in the unprivileged container can mount a bundle. The install path is only exercised on
   the board, one failure at a time, so each flash should be preceded by reading what the
   next step needs, as was done here.
